#!/usr/bin/python3
# Generated by Ask CK PyTest Creator for AWPTCM-T33351 — (188) Authentication&Security_IEEE 802.1X -  Single host
# Standardized ART framework script. Frame is fixed; test logic is filled per step.
#
# ==== OBJECTIVE — expected results this script must demonstrate ====
#   - In single-host mode, a supplicant successfully authenticates using 802.1X (dot1x)
#   against the configured RADIUS server and is granted network access on the port.
#   - After successful authentication in single-host mode, the supplicant is placed into the
#   VLAN assigned by RADIUS or the configured Guest VLAN.
#   - Unauthenticated traffic (prior to successful 802.1X authentication) is blocked on a
#   port in single-host mode; only EAPOL frames are permitted.
#   - The port correctly transitions to the authorized state for the single supplicant and
#   reports the assigned VLAN and auth status in show commands.
#   - Configuring single-host mode with "auth host-mode single-host" (combined with dot1x
#   port-control auto) is accepted and the mode is accurately reflected in running
#   configuration and operational state.
#   - Upon receipt of an EAP-Logoff from the authenticated supplicant in single-host mode,
#   the port returns to the unauthorized state, an EAP-Failure is sent, and the change is
#   logged and visible.
#   - Unsupported dynamic VLAN creation commands (e.g. auth dynamic-vlan-creation type multi
#   on single-host) are rejected with an appropriate error.
#   - 802.1X configuration including host-mode, RADIUS servers, and related timers persists
#   in running/startup config and is restored after reload where supported.
#   - The switch handles the maximum supported number of 802.1X clients and correctly
#   performs dynamic VLAN assignment for authenticated single-host supplicants.
# ==================================================================

